            <div xml:id="d1485">

                <pb facs="1196" n="1080" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1080"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/257.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Nicaraguan Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-11-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 11, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 7th instant, in which you inform me that a contract
                    [etc.]</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to inform you that the name of Clifford D. Ham, at
                    present Surveyor of the Port of Manila, has been placed in nomination by Messrs.
                    Brown Brothers and Company and J. and W. Seligman and Company to fill the post
                    of Collector-General of Customs of Nicaragua, and that I have this day approved
                    his nomination as a suitable and competent person to fill that position.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
